────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Bundled / downloaded third-party binaries
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The desktop build ships or downloads the following executables. They are
invoked as separate processes (the app talks to them over pipes and the
filesystem); they are not linked into Tatakai's own code.

1. FFmpeg / ffprobe
   Delivered through `@ffmpeg-installer/ffmpeg` and
   `@ffprobe-installer/ffprobe`. The licence of the shipped binary depends on
   the platform build published by those packages, and it is *not* uniform:

     linux-x64   ffmpeg GPLv3        ffprobe GPL-3.0
     win32-x64   ffmpeg GPLv3        ffprobe GPL-3.0
     darwin-x64  ffmpeg LGPL-2.1     ffprobe GPL-3.0

   Project: https://ffmpeg.org — source: https://ffmpeg.org/download.html
   Copying / redistribution of a GPL build carries the obligations of that
   licence (including the licence text and the source-availability terms). If
   you redistribute a Tatakai build, check which platform packages it contains
   and satisfy those obligations for the exact binaries you ship — being
   separate executables changes what *you* must do, not whether the licence
   applies. This note is descriptive, not legal advice.

2. libvips (through `sharp`)
   `sharp` links libvips, which is licensed LGPL-3.0-or-later, and the
   prebuilt `@img/sharp-*` packages bundle it. Project:
   https://www.libvips.org — licence: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.html

3. UnRAR
   If an UnRAR binary is present on a user's system, Tatakai only calls it to
   list/extract archives the user selected. UnRAR's own licence forbids using
   it to re-create the RAR compression algorithm; Tatakai does not do that and
   does not bundle UnRAR.

4. Rust dependencies (`translate-engine/`)
   See `translate-engine/Cargo.lock` and `cargo license` for the full crate
   graph. Crates are statically linked into the translate engine, so their
   notices apply to that binary.

5. Localisation model weights (Qwen3-VL and friends)
   Downloaded at the user's request into the app data directory, not shipped
   in the installer. Each model carries its own licence (Apache-2.0 for the
   Qwen3-VL family at the time of writing) — the model card is authoritative
   for the version you download.

